Summary
11 of 26 columns map cleanly to a live-verified SICS source or a proven derivation: CLA_BK, CLA_DESC, CLA_TYPE (default ATT), CLA_STATUS, CLA_STATUS_CODE, CLA_LOSS_DATE, CLA_REPORTED_DATE, CLA_LAST_TRANSACTION, CLA_IS_MOVEMENT, CLST_SRGT, LSTP_SRGT.

10 of 26 columns have a plausible source that is empty or only partly proven here: CLA_BROKER, CLA_SOURCE, CLA_HANDLER, CLA_ALT_REF, CLA_OPEN_DATE / CLA_REOPEN_DATE / CLA_CLOSE_DATE, CLGRP_SRGT, CLSS_SRGT, CLTP_SRGT, CLSTP_SRGT.

2 of 26 columns are weak: POLICY_SRGT (join), and the unused LRG amount input inside CLA_TYPE.

3 of 26 columns are DW-only: CLA_CLAIM_SRGT, CREATED_DATE_SRGT, UPDATED_DATE_SRGT.

This SICS copy has no claim ledger and no headline loss. CLA_TYPE therefore always defaults to ATT. CLA_SOURCE stays null until classification 528 is populated. Grain is claim–section unless ETL collapses OC202210000 to one row. Status / substatus / loss-type codes need translation to legacy DW values (O→OP, numeric cause codes vs 135).

 

